;; Package x86i is Arbace's x86-64 machine (doc/asm/AMD64.md §10; AX5-DESIGN, AXS51-AXS62): a Linux process's integer
;; instructions interpreted over emu's address space and kernel, decoded by LLVM's X86 disassembler rebuilt from the table
;; (decode.go over dgen's dectab.go), each mnemonic's family hand-written from the Intel SDM and the AMD APM as references
;; (sem.go), the flags computed lazily (flags.go). An instruction no family claims raises SIGILL with the class
;; :unimplemented, never a silent wrong result.
(in-ns 'go.arbace.x86i) (go/file "cpu.go" :doc "Package x86i is Arbace's x86-64 machine (doc/asm/AMD64.md §10; AX5-DESIGN, AXS51-AXS62): a Linux process's integer\ninstructions interpreted over emu's address space and kernel, decoded by LLVM's X86 disassembler rebuilt from the table\n(decode.go over dgen's dectab.go), each mnemonic's family hand-written from the Intel SDM and the AMD APM as references\n(sem.go), the flags computed lazily (flags.go). An instruction no family claims raises SIGILL with the class\n:unimplemented, never a silent wrong result.\n" :imports [


    ^{:line 9} [fmt "fmt"]
    ^{:line 10} [strings "strings"]

    ^{:line 12} [emu "arbace/emu"]])



